@@ -19,3 +19,21 @@ resolvePointer({ a: { b: [1, 2, 3] } }, "/a/b/1"); // 2
 
 Throws if `pointer` is not a syntactically valid JSON Pointer, or if it does not resolve to a value
 within `document`.
+
+### `applyPatch(document, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) — an array of `add`, `remove`,
+`replace`, `move`, `copy` or `test` operations — to a JSON document and returns the resulting
+document. `document` is left untouched; the result is a new value.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]);
+// { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
+
+Throws if `patch` is not a valid JSON Patch (e.g. an operation is missing a required member, or has
+an unknown `op`), or if applying one of its operations fails (e.g. it targets a location that does
+not exist, a `move` would relocate a value into one of its own children, or a `test` operation does
+not match).
